`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Every route: test larger, then validate at target scale"}),`
`]}),e.jsx(j,{}),e.jsxs(n,{title:"Every route ends with a check at target scale",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The figure shows one route per row, read from left to right. Transfer rules, the top row, change how the model is parametrized, so that a setting tuned on a small proxy model carries over as the model gets wider ",e.jsx(s,{id:"yang2022mup",children:"Yang et al., 2021"}),". The next tab teaches one such set of rules, μP. Width is not the only thing that grows, so the learning rate still needs corrections for the training length and the batch size."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Fitted laws, the middle row, leave the parametrization as it is. You tune the learning rate and the batch size on a ladder of small runs: a series of models of increasing size trained with one recipe. You then fit how the best learning rate ",e.jsx(a,{math:"\\eta^*",display:!1})," and batch size ",e.jsx(a,{math:"B^*",display:!1})," move with the model size ",e.jsx(a,{math:"N",display:!1})," and the number of training tokens ",e.jsx(a,{math:"D",display:!1,trail:"."})," Then you extrapolate to the target."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The bottom row combines the two routes, as the Delphi recipe does. Delphi comes from Marin, a community project whose code, checkpoints and tracking issues are public. In Delphi the optimizer takes care of changes in model width. A separate term in the learning rate, set from small runs, takes care of changes in the number of training tokens ",e.jsx(s,{id:"held2026delphi",children:"Held, 2026"}),"."]}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Every route should end in the same two checks. First, test the recipe on larger runs that the fit has not seen. A miss there costs far less than a failed target run. Second, validate the chosen settings at the target scale, even after the larger runs succeed. Every transfer and every fit holds only for its optimizer, its numerical precision and the rest of its recipe. The target run is the first place where these conditions all meet at full size. In our reading, validating there means checking its loss against the forecast as it trains, with a stopping rule fixed in advance."})]})]})]}),`
